2:1-17 (* "There are no implicit conversions", and there was one more, for a\n   constant on its way from a DEFINITION to its own IMPLEMENTATION.  The\n   checker entered a unit's constants unit by unit, and an\n   implementation was given only the ones it declared itself.  A\n   constant of its definition was a name of unknown type there, and\n   unknown never diagnoses.  So this compiled, in the released 0.13.0\n   too, and Wait answered 1 for a constant of 1.5.  A CLIENT writing `n\n   := m.Half` was refused, and so was the same assignment from a\n   constant declared in the implementation.\n\n   `m9c --review` showed it on 2026-10-02: the page for Http listed\n   MaxWait, a constant of Http's definition, as "passed over, a type\n   unknown" at each of the three places its implementation used it.  A\n   measure before it was closed found 430 M9 files in this repository\n   and four applications, 274 of which the compiler accepts; none leaned\n   on it. *)
comments=2
